  "qualification_observations": [
    "Initial focused SDK calls exposed synchronous Django ORM execution on the FastMCP async loop; handlers were moved to database threads without disabling async safety. Focused checks then passed 72 tests.",
    "The first full marked suite passed 1624 tests. The actual stdio workflow then found that a denied inactive actor call omitted its known identity; attribution was repaired and the final full suite and actual protocol workflow passed.",
    "Regression coverage includes grant/scope revocation during reads, audit reservation/completion failure, invalid identifiers, administrator HTTP permissions, atomic CLI/admin rollback, fabricated approvals and blocked SDK network constructors.",
    "The real protocol qualification now runs in the existing disposable CI browser/API job. Native data, round, timeout, assertion, skip and coverage budgets were preserved.",
    "Final review added target account/dataset IDs to grant snapshots so administrator changes remain attributable after target deletion. That exact backend source passed the full marked suite and actual stdio workflow; frontend and browser/API behavior is unchanged."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Installation-controlled stdio identity is not authenticated per-client remote identity; shared local hosts share the configured actor. HTTP/SSE transports are blocked.",
    "MCP grants do not supply browser/REST project authorization, reviewer roles or a common telemetry/embedding/inference egress policy.",
    "Proposals and signed bundles confer no exact action approval; direct MCP mutation and expert Python remain blocked pending their required authority/isolation.",
    "Database audit is not cryptographically signed or immutable against the database administrator; retention, distributed recovery, PostgreSQL deployment and threat-model qualification remain open.",
    "Completion is recorded before output release, not as a receipt of delivery. In-flight revocation is rechecked before completion; already delivered data cannot be recalled.",
    "D18-D26 remain planned; prior packets, canonical queue and release/customer/value gates are preserved."
  ],
